\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Breaking the R-matrix into its parts: plain BCE, consistency loss during training (Eq.~\ref {eq:hierloss}), reconciliation at inference (Eq.~\ref {eq:reconcile}), and both. The consistency loss alone never beats plain BCE. On ArXiv the best arm is reconciliation alone; on cellcycle\_FUN reconciliation alone matches plain BCE and only the combination helps. These are independent single-seed runs, so absolute values may differ slightly from Table~\ref {tab:ablation}.}}{17}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decomp}{{8}{17}{Breaking the R-matrix into its parts: plain BCE, consistency loss during training (Eq.~\ref {eq:hierloss}), reconciliation at inference (Eq.~\ref {eq:reconcile}), and both. The consistency loss alone never beats plain BCE. On ArXiv the best arm is reconciliation alone; on cellcycle\_FUN reconciliation alone matches plain BCE and only the combination helps. These are independent single-seed runs, so absolute values may differ slightly from Table~\ref {tab:ablation}}{figure.caption.18}{}}
